# `existential-method` where a function's bound asks a trait of a packed value and one of
# the trait's methods gives the trait's type inside another type, here under an
# associated type (Jimmy's ruling EX, by Rust's rule for a `dyn` trait's methods; Type
# System ch. 3, "Existentials", "Associated types"): the packed value's dictionary has no
# entry for `Zero`, and no type to give for `Unit` of the hidden type, so `Measure`,
# which may call any method of `^Weighed`, is not applied to a packed value. `Weigh` is
# asked of the packed value itself and is fine. Expected text derived by hand from the
# ruling. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

trait ^Weighed a:
    type Unit
    Weigh: fn a -> Nat
    Zero: fn a -> Unit a

impl ^Weighed Nat:
    type Unit = Text
    fn Weigh n = n
    fn Zero n = ""

Hide: fn Nat -> any ^Weighed
fn Hide n = any n

Measure: fn a -> Nat where a: ^Weighed
fn Measure x = Weigh x

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Weigh (Hide 3)} {Measure (Hide 3)}")
